# No live agent evals by default

Caerus live evals consume the user's Gemini monthly quota (~1000 requests).

## Never do these unless the user explicitly requests it in the current turn

- Set `CAERUS_ALLOW_LIVE=1`
- Run `pytest -m live`
- Run `caerus eval run ...`
- Call agents (`parse_jd`, `research_company`, `select_resume`, `generate_cover_letter`, `orchestrate`) against real Gemini for "just checking"

## Always safe

- `pytest` / `pytest -m "not live"`
- Unit tests under `tests/` that mock `generate_structured` / `generate_text`
- `caerus eval list`
- Editing fixtures under `tests/fixtures/`

If unsure whether a command hits Gemini or Serper/Tavily, do not run it — ask the user.
